---
// REVIEW: Layer 2 interpretation for the Malmö POTS Symptom Score (MAPS),
// drafted for Craig's review. Static, rendered at build time. FAQ answers come
// from malmo-pots-score.content.ts and are shown word for word (they also feed
// the page's FAQPage JSON-LD).
import { FAQ, REFERENCE, SOURCES } from '../../tools/malmo-pots-score.content';
import RelatedTools from '../RelatedTools.astro';
import '../../styles/interpretation.css';

const s = SOURCES;
---

<!-- REVIEW: new copy for Craig's review. -->
<section class="interpretation" aria-labelledby="understanding-maps">
	<h2 id="understanding-maps">Understanding your MAPS score</h2>

	<h3 id="what-it-measures">What the score measures</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.measures.a}</p>
	<p>
		The symptoms are those reported by at least 75% of 4,835 people in an international POTS survey
		(<a href={s.spahic.href} rel="noopener">{s.spahic.label}</a>).
	</p>
	<p>{FAQ.compass.a}</p>

	<h3 id="score-bands">Malmö POTS score interpretation</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.high.a}</p>
	<table class="interp-table">
		<caption>Average MAPS totals in published studies</caption>
		<thead>
			<tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">People</th><th scope="col">Average</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			{REFERENCE.map(r => (
				<tr><th scope="row">{r.group}</th><td>{r.n}</td><td>{r.mean}</td><td><a href={s[r.source].href} rel="noopener">{s[r.source].label}</a></td></tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>
		The POTS group was small and highly selected, from one specialist centre, and the authors say the score still needs
		testing elsewhere. Treat 42 as a guide, not a line.
	</p>

	<h3 id="change">What a change in score means</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.change.a}</p>
	<p>
		Rating weekly or fortnightly around a treatment change gives a usable trend, and your saved results above keep it on
		this device. The <a href="/tools/trackers/symptom-diary/">symptom diary</a> can hold the day-to-day detail.
	</p>

	<h3 id="what-it-does-not-measure">What it does not measure</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.diagnosis.a}</p>
	<p>
		For the heart rate side, use the <a href="/tools/nasa-lean-test/">NASA lean test</a> and the
		<a href="/evidence/30-bpm-threshold-pots/">30 bpm threshold explainer</a>.
	</p>

	<h3 id="taking-it-to-your-gp">Taking this to your GP or consultant</h3>
	<p>
		Bring your total, the date, your highest-rated symptoms and the trend from your saved results. Most GPs will not know
		MAPS: describe it as a 12-symptom POTS questionnaire from Lund University (<em>J Intern Med</em> 2023), where 42 or
		more separated POTS from healthy controls. It supports asking for a lying and standing heart rate and blood pressure
		check, alongside any lean test readings, but is not evidence of a diagnosis. See
		<a href="/testing/preparing-for-gp-appointment/">preparing for a GP appointment</a>.
	</p>

	<RelatedTools path="/tools/malmo-pots-score/" />

	<div class="tool-foot">
		<slot name="disclaimer" />
		<details class="sources" id="sources">
			<summary>Sources and licence</summary>
			<slot name="citation" />
			<ul class="interp-sources">
				<li>Spahic JM, Hamrefors V, Johansson M, Ricci F, Melander O, Sutton R, Fedorowski A. Malmö POTS symptom score: assessing symptom burden in postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome. <em>J Intern Med</em> 2023;293(1):91–99. <a href={s.spahic.href} rel="noopener">Full text</a></li>
				<li>Stick M, et al. Deep abdominal breathing reduces heart rate and symptoms during orthostatic challenge in patients with postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome. <em>Eur J Neurol</em> 2024;31:e16402. <a href={s.stick.href} rel="noopener">Full text</a></li>
			</ul>
		</details>
	</div>
</section>
